how's everybody doing today you may have  noticed quite a few new players hopping  in a fortnight lately maybe even people  haven't played a lot of video games  we're gonna talk about six common  mistakes that players make in the game  and how to get a little bit better  let's talk games number one not mapping  building to hotkeys the default controls  in fortnight are way too slow and will  likely get you killed you should have at  least walls and ramps map when combined  they make the fastest for it's never  just build one layer of walls have  fallback walls just in case because  other teams will shoot them about as  fast as you can put them up while you're  at it map your first weapon slot to an  easy to reach mouse button or heat you  never want to die with your pickaxe out  that's kind of embarrassing as you run  across the map practice switching  between weapons and building to get  those hotkeys in your muscle memory  number two forgetting to build under  fire it's easy to panic when the Rockets  start flying but taking a second to set  yourself up with a couple of walls can  make a huge difference wood starts with  more initial hit points and can take  more hits while being constructed brick  and steel have higher max hit points and  can take a lot more punishment when  completed when enemy teams try and ramp  up and over your forts build ramps to  the same plane height as them in order  to engage or if you're fast enough shoot  out the base of their ramp to make the  whole thing collapse most importantly  make sure to harvest enough resources at  the start of a round if you get to the  end circles and can't put up walls or  ramps you're probably a goner  number three  forgetting to knock down enemy forts  chop down enemy forts as they're built  preferably at the base to bleed enemy  teams resources and open them up if you  do manage to chop out the base of a  tower the entire thing will fall don't  expect anything you hide behind a hold  though almost all objects can be  destroyed number four landing in hot  spots if you want to go to tilted towers  to learn how to fight that's one thing  but if you're playing to make it to the  late-game this might be a bad idea  Landing areas that are rich in loot and  aren't as likely to see fights early on  such as shifty shafts or moisty mire no  promises though also don't land on a  house second if someone beats you to the  ground definitely move somewhere else in  town so you have plenty of room to get  arms winning a pickaxe fight is dicey at  best assuming one of you doesn't have a  weapon number five  forgetting to share health items  scattered around the map our blue shield  potions and bandages you should drink  shield oceans right away to build up a  second layer of shields but anything  extra that you find you should give to a  friend you can actually drop or simply  divide out shields and bandages from  your inventory menu if your team goes  down you're a lot more likely to lose  anyway so there's little reason to horde  what you find number six  picking the wrong weapon don't let the  cartoonish style fool you treat every  gunfight in this game like it's your  last you don't need to hold back because  if you win you should have plenty of  weapons to scavenge anyway remember when  picking up items not all weapons in  fortnight are created equal there are  color variations from gray to gold that  indicate their power so for example  ditch green for blue blue for purple  purple for orange and so on make sure  you understand the ideal range of  weapons don't shoot the wrong gun at the  wrong range or you'll just let people  know you're there but also keep in mind  that shotguns have more range than you  think and are some of the most powerful  weapons in the game some guns look great  like the new minigun and they are great  at chopping down forts but are pretty  lousy at killing players overall just  make sure you practice enough to know  what guns are good with  alright those are some of the most  common mistakes we've seen new players  making in fortnight what about you tell  us some of the things you see new  players doing what are your favorite  landing zones let's talk about it in the  comments below thanks for watching
 

